.TH PAPERWEIGHT\-NETWORK 1 "2026-11-08" "paperweight-skel 0.2.87" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paperweight\-network \- pick and connect to a Wi\-Fi network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paperweight\-network
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paperweight\-network
lists the Wi\-Fi networks NetworkManager can see in a
.BR yad (1)
window, with signal strength, security type, and a check mark next to the
network you are connected to.
Pick one to connect.
.PP
If the network is secured, a password prompt follows.
The result is shown as a desktop notification.
Once connected, NetworkManager remembers the network and its password as
usual.
.PP
It is bound to
.B Super+N
(\fB$mod+n\fR) and is the
.B Network
entry in
.BR paperweight\-settings (1).
For anything beyond picking a network (VPNs, wired settings, forgetting a
network), use
.BR nmtui (1),
which opens when you click the network icon in the bar.
.SH NOTES
The list comes from NetworkManager's most recent scan, so a network that
has just appeared may take a few seconds to show up.
SSIDs that contain a colon are not parsed correctly.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmcli (1),
.BR nmtui (1),
.BR paperweight\-settings (1)
